@startuml cgms_fault_handling
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title CGMS Fault Handling Architecture (Updated)

component "Glucose Sensor" as Sensor
component "MCU / Firmware" as MCU
component "Diagnostics Manager" as Diag
component "Fault Manager" as Fault
component "Lifecycle Manager" as Life
component "Alert Manager" as Alert
component "Mobile App" as App
component User

' --------------------
' Fault detection
' --------------------
Sensor --> MCU : abnormal signal / missing data
MCU --> Diag : signal quality metrics

' --------------------
' Fault classification
' --------------------
Diag --> Fault : fault candidate
Fault --> Fault : classify (transient / terminal)

' --------------------
' Escalation & enforcement
' --------------------
Fault --> Life : terminal fault?
Life --> MCU : invalidate measurements

' --------------------
' User notification
' --------------------
Fault --> Alert : fault state
Alert --> App : BLE notify(fault)
App --> User : sensor error / replace sensor

note right of Diag
Detection sources:
- Sensor drift
- Signal saturation
- Temperature out-of-range
- ADC anomalies
end note

note right of Fault
Fault handling:
- Debounce / persistence
- Escalation rules
- Terminal vs recoverable
end note

note right of Life
Terminal faults:
- Force Expired state
- No recovery allowed
end note

note bottom of Alert
Regulatory:
ISO 14971 Risk Control
Fault alarms override
glucose alarms
end note

@enduml

